From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:01:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: Add the Apple T6041 AOP audio

Describe the T6041 AOP's audio child, which the AOP binding leaves a
bare object: the compatible, the ADMAC channels by name (the
microphones' "dma", the speakers' "spkr" and "sense", and the optional
headset jack's "cout" and "cin"), the chassis and machine names of the
microphone card, and "#sound-dai-cells", whose values 3 and 4 select
the AOP audio driver's speaker and headset jack back-ends.

The schema is modelled on the T8140 one, and the AOP binding's audio
child references it.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
